  "name": "acid rain",
  "bpm": 138,
  "ticksPerBeat": 4,
  "length": 128,
  "loop": {
   "start": 0,
   "end": 128
  },
  "info": "Eight bars of acid techno at 138 bpm from five machines (a kick, a hi-hat, a clap, a 303-style squelch bassline and a comb-resonator metal percussion), all played by one meta machine, with a spacer and the machine's name between the groups of columns. The drums start alone, the acid line comes in at bar 3 with its filter nearly closed and opens up through the song (cutoff every other tick, then resonance, envelope amount, decay and drive each bar), the claps and the metal join at bar 5, and a hat and clap roll closes the loop. The squelch has accents (Acc, the accent column) and slides (Sld): a slide glides into the note from the one before. The metal is a relative note column: 80 is E-5."
 },
